<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><h1 class="st-title">Beylik of Constantine</h1><p class="st-meta">1567 CE – 1837 CE (approx.) · capital Constantine</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The eastern province of Ottoman Algiers, the largest and richest, whose last bey made Constantine the final stronghold against the French.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/regency-of-algiers">Regency of Algiers</a> organised the eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beylik">beylik</a> in 1567, with its seat in the ancient rock-top city of Constantine. It covered eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeria">Algeria</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kabylia">Kabylia</a> to the Tunisian border and south to the Saharan oases such as <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sultanate-of-touggourt">Touggourt</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The beys ruled through local great families and makhzen tribes, collecting taxes in grain, wool and livestock and paying heavy tribute to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algiers">Algiers</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salah-bey">Salah Bey</a>, who ruled from 1771 to 1792, built mosques, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madrasa">madrasas</a> and bridges and is remembered in local song. Constantine was a centre of learning, crafts and leather work.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algiers">Algiers</a> fell in 1830, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmed-bey-of-constantine">Ahmed Bey</a> held Constantine and repulsed a French assault in 1836. The French stormed the city in October 1837, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beylik">beylik</a> was absorbed into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/french-algeria">French Algeria</a>; Ahmed Bey fought on until 1848.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/beylik-of-constantine.jpg" alt="Beylik of Constantine" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: Nourerrahmane · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Beylik_of_Constantina.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1567 CE – 1837 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Constantine</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Salah Bey, Ahmed Bey</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic, Berber, Ottoman Turkish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/algeria">Algeria</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Constantine beylik, Beylik of the East</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1702&amp;focus=beylik-of-constantine" aria-label="Beylik of Constantine on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4846 866 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Beylik of Constantine lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5166 1122L5077 1108M5166 1122L5077 1108"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5077 1108h0M5077 1108h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5166 1122h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5166 1122h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Constantine. <a href="/atlas?year=1702&amp;focus=beylik-of-constantine">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

